# =============================================================================
# public/_redirects — canonicalization for the Cloudflare Pages project
# serving BOTH posternlabs.com AND posternpool.com.
#
# Cloudflare _redirects notes:
#   - Format:  <source>  <destination>  <status>   (one rule per line)
#   - A source that includes a scheme+host matches on the incoming hostname,
#     which is what lets us fold "www" into the apex per-domain.
#   - :splat carries only the PATH through to a FIXED, hard-coded destination
#     host. There is NO user-controlled host in any destination, so these
#     cannot be abused as an open redirect.
#   - Cloudflare Pages already forces http -> https on its own; no rule needed.
#   - Both apexes are kept DISTINCT on purpose — posternpool.com is NOT folded
#     into posternlabs.com. We only collapse each domain's "www" onto its apex.
# =============================================================================

# www -> apex (301 permanent), per domain, path preserved.
https://www.posternlabs.com/*   https://posternlabs.com/:splat   301
https://www.posternpool.com/*   https://posternpool.com/:splat   301

# Bare short URL -> canonical Gramota app path. Anyone who types or is handed
# the short form /gramota should land on the real app at /apps/gramota/ (which
# serves <title>Gramota — enterprise onboarding · Postern Labs</title>) instead
# of falling through to index.html with a misleading 200. Path-only, fixed
# destination, no user-controlled host: not an open redirect.
/gramota    /apps/gramota/   301


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploy-time caveats (these rules are inert / harmless until the conditions
# are met, so they cannot break anything if unmet):
#   - Each "www" host must actually be attached to the Pages project as a
#     custom domain (or CNAME'd to it) for its redirect to ever fire.
#   - If you instead prefer apex -> www as canonical, swap the two sides.
#   - Intentionally NOT added: any rewrite of posternpool.com's "/" to the pool
#     page. Same project => posternpool.com/ currently serves index.html (the
#     Labs home). If pool.com should land on /pool/ or /pool.html, that's a
#     content-routing decision for the site owner — add e.g.
#       https://posternpool.com/   /pool.html   200
#     deliberately, not as a security change.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# NOTE: the old "/pool -> / 301" and "/pool.html -> / 301" rules were REMOVED
# (2026-07-15) — there is now a real Pool page (site/pool.html -> /pool.html and
# /pool/). Redirecting them to home broke the nav's Pool button.

# The React wallet PWA at /apps/mobile-wallet-pwa/ was UNPUBLISHED (2026-07-18):
